54
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.390
First and foremost, the music.

55
00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.160
I mean..
It's so weird to hear.

56
00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.596
I don't know how he looks older then than he does now.

57
00:01:59.596 --> 00:02:00.770
(Ross laughs)

58
00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.600
But listen, we all know where that went.

59
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.920
He changed the world.

60
00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.860
He's the king of all media and he grew his signature persona

61
00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.250
and his full body take no prisoners interviewing style.

62
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:16.250
And he became the most fined radio host in FCC history.

63
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:19.600
After a 44-year career, he's still going strong.

64
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.800
And I remember the first time that I was interviewed by him.

65
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.665
I've interviewed people for 20 years now.

66
00:02:23.665 --> 00:02:26.600
And I thought to myself after he interviewed me,

67
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.530
I thought I'm such a better interviewer

68
00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:31.810
because of what I just sat there and saw him do.

69
00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.800
He's so well-researched

70
00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.810
and yet he leads it as a disarming conversation.

71
00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.680
There is no one better in the business than Howard Stern.

72
00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.300
And who knew a shock jock who made 96 bucks a week

73
00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.500
would become the interview of a lifetime.

74
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.160
If you are lucky enough to be in his hot seat,

75
00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.240
well, you're very lucky and I...

76
00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.550
Hats off to Howard Stern.

77
00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.230
The best of the best, Howard.

78
00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.063
All right, next.

79
00:02:57.063 --> 00:03:00.160
Don't never say never, ever, ever, ever, ever.

80
